<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agra is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna River</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was one of the main capitals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, home to the Agra Fort and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taj-mahal">Taj Mahal</a>, built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a>. It was also an important commercial centre within the Mughal economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agra.jpg" alt="Agra" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yann · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taj_Mahal,_Agra,_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Lodi recovery under Bahlul and Sikandar was genuine but limited, never regaining the Deccan or Bengal, though Sikandar founded <b>Agra</b> as a new capital in 1504.</blockquote><a href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The great majority of the population were peasants producing staples such as wheat, rice and cotton, while cities such as <b>Agra</b>, Delhi and Lahore functioned as hubs of commerce and administration.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>For the tomb he chose land south of <b>Agra</b> on which a mansion of Raja Jai Singh I stood, and Jai Singh gave it to him in exchange for a large palace in the centre of the city.</blockquote><a href="/work/taj-mahal">Taj Mahal · Origins</a></li><li><blockquote>In law the emperor was the final judge: Jahangir hung a “chain of justice” in the <b>Agra</b> Fort that any wronged subject could shake.</blockquote><a href="/societies/mughal-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Mughal Empire</a></li><li><blockquote>Shah Jahan commissioned the Taj Mahal in <b>Agra</b> to house her tomb.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-17">17 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Jat peasant leaders around Mathura and <b>Agra</b> rose against Mughal authority in the late 17th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/bharatpur-state">Bharatpur State</a></li></ul></section>
